    "body": "## Summary\n- expose the existing backend worker evidence policy in the job attachment UI\n- allow the assigned worker to upload only `PARTICIPANTS` attachments while a job is exactly `IN_PROGRESS`\n- pin worker uploads to participant-only visibility so the browser cannot suggest broader permissions the API rejects\n- label the worker flow explicitly for receipts/expense evidence and document the privacy boundary\n\n## Why\nThe backend already supports receipt-backed expense claims and, since #105, permits the assigned worker to upload participant-only evidence during execution. The web UI still restricted uploads to the requester, which made the commercial expense flow impossible to complete through the product UI. This slice aligns frontend capabilities with the existing server-side authorization without widening any backend permission.\n\n## Migration\nNo Flyway migration is required.\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until every required check for the exact latest head is complete and green. Fix any failure on this same branch.",
